{{Yearbox/in-conflicts}}
* The [[War of Gold and Gloom]] comes to an end when the [[Army of Gold]] discovers the long-forgotten history of [[Clan Duergar]], which precipitates an attack from an army of [[illithid]] thralls. The [[duergar]] and [[gold dwarf]] armies join with each other to repel the army and the duergar take the most casualties. The Army of Gold offers an alliance to what remains of the [[Army of Steel]] and the united dwarves march to retake [[Shanatar]] where they hope to be better prepared to repel the inevitable second attack from [[Oryndoll]].<ref name="GHotR-159" />
* The [[Shadowbane War]] occurs when [[Netheril#Empire_of_Shadows|Netheril]] attacks the [[Zhentarim]].<ref name="MotA-65">{{Cite dungeon/170/Monument of the Ancients|65}}</ref><ref group="note">The name of the [[Shadowbane War]] and its date of [[1383 DR]] are given in ''[[Dungeon magazine]]'' [[Dungeon magazine 170|Issue #170]]: ''[[Monument of the Ancients]]'', in which the only additional information provided is that [[Cvaal Daoran]] killed a [[shade]] prince. It is not explicitly stated to be the same as the broader conflict between [[Netheril#Empire_of_Shadows|Netheril]] and the [[Zhentarim]] mentioned in other sources, and [[canon]] material does not explicitly name or date the conflict elsewhere. However, the author of ''Monument of the Ancients'', [[Brian R. James]], clarified in a [https://web.archive.org/web/20230420160236/https://twitter.com/brianrjames/status/1696164904?s=46&t=xaFHtQctnID1KcLCd6DOzg Tweet] that the broader conflict indeed occurred in 1383 DR. Thus, the Shadowbane War is presumed to be the name for the broader conflict.</ref> [[Zhentil Keep]] and the [[Citadel of the Raven]] are destroyed, and the Zhentarim's power over the [[Moonsea]] is broken.<ref name="FRCG-p282">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide|282}}</ref><ref name="FRCG-p150">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide|150}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-people}}
* [[Cvaal Daoran]] of [[Phlan]] single-handedly slays a [[Prince of Shade]] during the Shadowbane War.<ref name="MotA-65" />

{{Yearbox/deaths}}
* [[Triel Baenre]] is murdered by her sister [[Quenthel Baenre|Quenthel]].<ref>{{Cite book/Menzoberranzan: City of Intrigue|37}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-deities}}
* The [[Morndinsamman]] openly attack [[Laduguer]] and [[Deep Duerra]]. Laduguer is killed by [[Moradin]]<ref name="GHotR-159" /> and Deep Duerra is killed by [[Clangeddin Silverbeard|Clangeddin]]<ref name="GHotR-159" /> but [[Gorm Gulthyn]] and [[Haela Brightaxe]] also die in the battle.<ref name="GHotR-159" /> Without the support of Laduguer and Deep Duerra, the plane of [[Hammergrim]] disperses into the [[Astral Plane]].<ref name="GHotR-159">{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|159}}</ref>
* [[Fzoul Chembryl]] is slain during the Netherese siege of Zhentil Keep and is elevated as an [[exarch]] by [[Bane]].<ref name="FRCG-p238">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide|238}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-organizations}}
* The [[ulitharid]] [[Galgast]] takes command of and revitalizes the [[Sept of Ill'Ghact]]. Plans begin to proceed apace with the stalled goal of restoring the city of [[Phanlinksal]].<ref>{{Cite book/Menzoberranzan: City of Intrigue|113}}</ref>
* [[House Horlbar]] and [[House Kenafin]], both accused of heresy, join forces, creating [[House Melarn (Menzoberranzan)|House Melarn]]. Named after [[Lolth]]'s [[Halisstra Melarn|Lady Penitent]], they (and many refugees from [[Ched Nasad]]) strive to prove themselves devout by intruding into the personal business of minor houses and exposing any perceived heresies to the public.<ref name="M.CoI-p48-49">{{Cite book/Menzoberranzan: City of Intrigue|48-49}}</ref>
* The [[Zhentarim]] breaks away from the influence of the [[Church of Bane]] following the death of Fzoul Chembryl, and the [[Church of Cyric]] attempts to fill the void.<ref name="FRCG-p282" />

{{Yearbox/in-politics}}
* Lord Protector Cvaal Daoran of Phlan forms a pact with the [[dark fey]] of the [[Quivering Forest]], gaining protection for Phlan in exchange for a promise to prohibit logging and travel in the forest.<ref name="MotA-81">{{Cite dungeon/170/Monument of the Ancients|81}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/misc}}
* The [[Durpar]]i city of [[Vaelan]] becomes renowned across [[Faerûn]] for its exotic body art which utilizes [[Plangent crystal|living crystal]] that also improves the talents of the subject.<ref name="GHotR-159" />
* This year is known as the Year of Unjust Rewards in the [[Black Chronology]].<ref name="C.TotW-159">{{Cite book/Cormyr: The Tearing of the Weave|159}}</ref><ref name="TGHotR-157">{{Cite book/The Grand History of the Realms|157}}</ref>

