* A mysterious cabal known as [[The Six]] launches attacks against [[Acquisitions Incorporated]] in the [[Sword Coast North]].<ref name="AI5e-p102">{{Cite book/Acquisitions Incorporated|102}}</ref>
* Ongoing conflicts escalate between the [[Xanathar's Thieves' Guild]] and the [[Zhentarim]] in [[Waterdeep]] amidst power grabs by groups like Acquisitions Incorporated.<ref name="AI5e-p82">{{Cite book/Acquisitions Incorporated|82}}</ref>
* Forces from the [[Far Realm]] attack the town of [[Red Larch]].<ref name="AI5e-p179">{{Cite book/Acquisitions Incorporated|179}}</ref>
* The [[red dragon]] [[Balagos]] captures and maims the [[bronze dragon]] [[Ixolothingeir]], and forces him to defend a secondary treasure hoard in the [[Starspire Mountains]].<ref name="HoF-p70">{{Cite book/Forgotten Realms: Heroes of Faerûn|70}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-organizations}}
* The splinter sect of the [[Zhentarim]] led by [[Manshoon]] seeks to solidify its power in the [[Sword Coast]]. The Zhent operative in [[Phandalin]], [[Halia Thornton]], is killed and replaced by a Manshoon loyalist named [[Sharna Quirstiron]], who plots to subvert the town's leaders.<ref name="AI5e-p106">{{Cite book/Acquisitions Incorporated|106}}</ref>
* Waterdeep's [[Guild of Chandlers and Lamplighters]] goes on strike, leaving the city dark and dangerous at night.<ref name="AI5e-p82" />
* The [[Blackstaff]], [[Vajra Safahr]], mobilizes the [[Gray Hands]] to determine the intentions of the [[green dragon]] [[Kofutacti]], who was spotted above the [[Sea of Swords]] near Waterdhavian shipping lanes.<ref name="AI5e-p82" />

{{Yearbox/in-politics}}
* The town of [[Phandalin]] holds its first mayoral election. The candidates are [[Harbin Wester]] and [[Sildar Hallwinter]].<ref name="AI5e-p101">{{Cite book/Acquisitions Incorporated|101}}</ref>

{{Yearbox/in-people}}
* Famous Waterdhavian actress [[Tystanya Creed]] disappears upon leaving the theater following a performance.<ref name="AI5e-p82" />
* A member of the [[nobility of Waterdeep]] in the [[Waterdeep/Southern Ward|Southern Ward]] survives an assassination attempt when a bodyguard injures the assailant. A bounty is offered for the would-be assassin's capture, but the only description given is that of a female [[half-elf]] with a wounded shoulder.<ref name="AI5e-p82" />

{{Yearbox/deaths}}
* [[Caerhan Coalsmith]] dies while trying to destroy the ''[[Orrery of the Wanderer]]''.<ref name="AI5e-p80-81">{{Cite book/Acquisitions Incorporated|80-81}}</ref>
* [[Halia Thornton]], proprietor of the [[Phandalin Miner's Exchange]] and a member of the [[Town Council of Phandalin]], is killed in secret. Many believe she has instead left town without saying why.<ref name="AI5e-p106" />

{{Yearbox/in-environment}}
* An earthquake rocks the city of [[Waterdeep]]. It is caused by the activation of a powerful shrine, dedicated to [[That-Which-Endures]], located in a tunnel system deep beneath the city.<ref name="AI5e-p80-81" />

{{Yearbox/misc}}
* Tall, black-cloaked skeletal figures are spotted at night in Waterdeep's [[Waterdeep/City of the Dead|City of the Dead]].<ref name="AI5e-p82" />
* A murderer in Waterdeep's [[Waterdeep/North Ward|North Ward]] attacks victims in broad daylight, severing their heads and feet. The feet are then taken by the killer.<ref name="AI5e-p82" />
* One of the [[Walking Statues of Waterdeep]] appears to start crying. Some see this as a sign of great misfortune, others as a sign of good luck, and others simply blame the humidity.<ref name="AI5e-p82" />

{{Yearbox/in-publications}}
